Update vendored crates flagged by RustSec to their newest semver-compatible
releases with `cargo update -p <crate>@<version>`:
  anyhow 1.0.102 -> 1.0.104 (RUSTSEC-2026-0190)
  crossbeam-epoch 0.9.18 -> 0.9.21 (RUSTSEC-2026-0204)
  h2 0.4.15 -> 0.4.20 (RUSTSEC-2026-0258)
  pulldown-cmark 0.13.3 -> 0.13.6 (RUSTSEC-2026-0414, -0433)
  rustix 1.1.4 -> 1.1.6 (RUSTSEC-2026-0486)
  rustls 0.23.45 -> 0.23.46 (RUSTSEC-2026-0346 to -0349)
  rustls-webpki 0.103.15 -> 0.103.17 (RUSTSEC-2026-0382)
  tokio 1.52.3 -> 1.54.1 (RUSTSEC-2026-0386)
  zstd 0.13.3 -> 0.13.5 (RUSTSEC-2026-0391)
  zstd-safe 7.2.4 -> 7.4.1 (RUSTSEC-2026-0395 to -0406)
  zstd-sys 2.0.16 -> 2.1.3 (RUSTSEC-2026-0410)
cargo also re-selected windows-sys 0.52.0 for a few Windows-only
dependency lists; both versions were already in the lockfile.

Not covered, as no semver-compatible release fixes it: scc 2.4
(RUSTSEC-2026-0205).

